  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppS&E 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'After a new cancer treatment is approved for wide use, the research
    team creates a national registry to track how patients are doing in everyday
    care settings.


    <b>Who typically helps manage and maintain this real-world
    data so it can be reviewed for safety and long-term outcomes?</b>'
  explanation: After a new treatment is approved, researchers and health systems
    often collect and manage real-world data through patient registries, surveys,
    and follow-up programs. This information helps identify patterns in side effects
    and outcomes and supports ongoing safety monitoring outside of clinical trials.
  correctAnswer: Researchers and health systems
  incorrectAnswer1: Institutional Review Board (IRB)
  incorrectAnswer2: Environmental Health & Safety (EHS)
  incorrectAnswer3: Scientific Review Committee (SRC)
  questionRole: Safety & Ethics
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Approval
